  "pli-tv-bu-vb-pc1:2.1.2": "Although <i lang='pi' translate='no'>muta</i> means “thought”, translating it as “sensed” is necessary in light of the definitions below. As for <i lang='pi' translate='no'>aviññāta</i>, “not mentally experienced”, the commentary at Sp 2.3 says: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Aññatra pañcahi indriyehi suddhena viññāṇeneva aggahitaṁ aviññātanti veditabbaṁ</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Aviññāta</i> is to be understood as what is grasped by mere consciousness apart from the five senses.” ",
